  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 7504.11 Failure to Surrender License, Plates, Registration",
  "priorExpiration": "2005-03-24",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 7504.11 Failure to Surrender License, Plates, Registration. In the event a person is advised by letter to surrender their license or registration certificate and plates, and such person fails to comply, the financial responsibility administrator or hearing examiner shall, after 15 working days from the effective date of the suspension or revocation, forward a pickup order to a law enforcement officer to retrieve such items.\n\nSource. #5274, eff 11-20-91; ss by #5688, eff 8-20-93; ss and moved by #6337, eff 9-25-96 (formerly Saf-C 206.10); amd by #7349, eff 8-22-00; amd by #8174, INTERIM, eff 9-25-04, EXPIRES: 3-24-05; ss moved by #8230-B, eff 12-17-04 (formerly Saf-C 207.10); ss by #10395-B, eff 8-15-13; ss by #13938, eff 4-24-24 (formerly Saf-C 207.11) (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Saf-C 7500)",
